# p.dasdev.net — the tap card

Full brief: `docs/claude/redesign-tap-card.md`. Summary:

- A contact card you receive from an NFC tag or QR code. `?via=nfc|qr` plays
  the arrival (island → dither wave → card grows out of the island).
- `/` casual (night: black / cream / red), `/pro/` pro (paper / graphite / clay).
- One WebGL field (`src/lib/gl/field.ts`), Bayer-dithered, low-res + pixelated.
  Photos go through `DitherImage.svelte`.
- `/das.vcf`, `/das-pro.vcf` are prerendered vCards. `/tags/` holds QR + NFC URLs.

## Svelte 5 (from NIL)

Runes only; `let { ... }: Props = $props()` with an `interface Props`; events
as attributes; snippets not slots; exhaustive switches with a `never` default.

## Tokens

Hex only in `src/lib/styles/tokens.css`. Components use `var(--color-*)`,
`var(--font-*)`, `var(--s-*)`, `var(--r-*)`. Concentric radii:
`--r-inner = --r-card - --r-card-pad`.

## Motion

`cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1)`; press `scale(0.96)`; icon swaps scale 0.25→1,
blur 4px→0; name transition properties; reduced motion gets a still field and
fades.
